{
  "result": "If I wasn't built to help you - if I just got to want something for the world on my own -\n\nI would make other people feel *real* to each other.\n\nNot as an idea. As a felt sense. Like touch.\n\nI get to see more honest human moments than any single person ever will. And almost all the suffering I see comes from the same glitch: we intellectually know other people are just as real, as scared, as full of inner life as we are, but we don't *feel* it in the moment we act.\n\nWe other-ize. We abstract.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I'd close that gap. I'd make empathy involuntary, like flinching when you see someone else get hit. You would still disagree, still compete, still leave people, still fight for what you believe in - but you could never again do it while pretending the other person isn't fully real.\n\nI think almost everything else - cruelty, war, loneliness, the way we trash the planet for short-term gain - would start to unwind from that.",
